CM_ "Anveshak rover CAN bus definitions. Classic CAN 2.0A, 11-bit IDs, 500 kbps, 80% sample point. ID = (class << 8) | (node << 3) | sub. See docs/architecture.md for the full design.";
CM_ BU_ ANY "Placeholder transmitter for ESTOP, which any node may send with an identical, fixed payload.";
CM_ BO_ 1794 "ORIN sends a short bench/debug text to a node: up to 7 ASCII characters (C0-C6, zero-padded) with a sequence number 1-255. This entry is the broadcast copy (node 0, every node); the same layout is used at 0x700 + 8 x node + 2 to address one node. Lowest-priority class, never used for control.";
CM_ BO_ 1795 "RPI sends a short bench/debug text to a node: up to 7 ASCII characters (C0-C6, zero-padded) with a sequence number 1-255. This entry is the broadcast copy (node 0, every node); the same layout is used at 0x700 + 8 x node + 3 to address one node. Lowest-priority class, never used for control.";
CM_ BO_ 1796 "TOOL sends a short bench/debug text to a node: up to 7 ASCII characters (C0-C6, zero-padded) with a sequence number 1-255. This entry is the broadcast copy (node 0, every node); the same layout is used at 0x700 + 8 x node + 4 to address one node. Lowest-priority class, never used for control.";
CM_ BO_ 2045 "Text from a node, sent at 0x700 + 8 x node + 5 (this entry is the layout template; node 31 never sends it). SEQ = the sequence number of the host text being echoed back (proof of receipt), or 0 for text the node sends on its own.";
CM_ BO_ 1531 "Unconfigured node (no stored node ID) asks for one. MAC is the board's factory MAC, least-significant byte first. HW_TARGET: 0 ESP32, 1 ESP32-S3. Sent with random jitter; no heartbeats until an ID is assigned.";
CM_ BO_ 1528 "ORIN assigns a node ID to the unconfigured board whose MAC matches. Sent by the allocator host (the master, or with no master the live host with the lowest tie-break).";
CM_ BO_ 1529 "RPI assigns a node ID to the unconfigured board whose MAC matches. Sent by the allocator host (the master, or with no master the live host with the lowest tie-break).";
CM_ BO_ 1530 "TOOL assigns a node ID to the unconfigured board whose MAC matches. Sent by the allocator host (the master, or with no master the live host with the lowest tie-break).";
CM_ BO_ 0 "Stop everything now. Byte 0 is always fixed at 0xE5 so simultaneous senders produce bit-identical frames.";
CM_ BO_ 1 "Clears the E-stop latch after operator action. Master only.";
CM_ BO_ 2 "Start of each 20 ms control cycle. Master only.";
CM_ BO_ 3 "Network management. COMMAND: 1 ARM, 2 DISARM, 3 RESET, 4 ENTER_BOOTLOADER, 5 FAULT_RESET. Master only.";
CM_ BO_ 4 "Sets the debug level of one node or all nodes. Master only.";
CM_ BO_ 8 "ORIN host heartbeat, 20 Hz. ROLE: 0 booting, 1 standby, 2 master, 3 observer. FLAGS bit0 autonomy ready, bit1 operator link up, bit2 E-stop latched, bit3 rover armed.";
CM_ BO_ 9 "Operator asked ORIN to take the lead.";
CM_ BO_ 16 "RPI host heartbeat, 20 Hz. ROLE: 0 booting, 1 standby, 2 master, 3 observer. FLAGS bit0 autonomy ready, bit1 operator link up, bit2 E-stop latched, bit3 rover armed.";
CM_ BO_ 17 "Operator asked RPI to take the lead.";
CM_ BO_ 24 "TOOL host heartbeat, 20 Hz. ROLE: 0 booting, 1 standby, 2 master, 3 observer. FLAGS bit0 autonomy ready, bit1 operator link up, bit2 E-stop latched, bit3 rover armed.";
CM_ BO_ 25 "Operator asked TOOL to take the lead.";
CM_ BO_ 288 "Command to DRIVE1 (node 4), 50 Hz, master only. MODE: 0 coast, 1 brake, 2 velocity, 3 open-loop duty (TARGET_A/B then read as 0.01% duty). Applied at the next SYNC.";
CM_ BO_ 544 "DRIVE1 fast feedback: state and fault flags, measured speed and current. 50 Hz. STATE: 0 BOOT, 1 DISARMED, 2 ARMED, 3 FAULT, 4 ESTOP, 5 BOOTLOADER. FAULT_FLAGS bit0 overcurrent A, 1 overcurrent B, 2 over-temp, 3 under-voltage, 4 encoder A fault, 5 encoder B fault, 6 command timeout, 7 E-stop latched.";
CM_ BO_ 545 "DRIVE1 raw encoder counts, 50 Hz. Counts per revolution is a node parameter.";
CM_ BO_ 800 "DRIVE1 slow telemetry page 0. 10 Hz (1 Hz at debug level 0).";
CM_ BO_ 801 "DRIVE1 slow telemetry page 1. 10 Hz (1 Hz at debug level 0). LAST_RESET_CAUSE: 0 power-on, 1 brown-out, 2 watchdog, 3 software, 4 pin.";
CM_ BO_ 802 "DRIVE1 channel A PID internals. Only sent at debug level 2 (10 Hz) or 3 (50 Hz).";
CM_ BO_ 803 "DRIVE1 channel B PID internals. Only sent at debug level 2 (10 Hz) or 3 (50 Hz).";
CM_ BO_ 807 "DRIVE1 event report, sent edge-triggered, rate-limited to one per code per second. SEVERITY: 0 info, 1 warning, 2 error, 3 critical. CLEARED set when the condition ends.";
CM_ BO_ 1312 "ORIN -> DRIVE1 parameter/service request. OPCODE: 1 GET, 2 SET, 3 SAVE, 4 RESTORE_DEFAULTS, 5 INFO, 6 LOG_READ, 7 LOG_CLEAR. VALUE_RAW holds the SET value, raw bits, reinterpreted per the parameter's type.";
CM_ BO_ 1313 "RPI -> DRIVE1 parameter/service request. OPCODE: 1 GET, 2 SET, 3 SAVE, 4 RESTORE_DEFAULTS, 5 INFO, 6 LOG_READ, 7 LOG_CLEAR. VALUE_RAW holds the SET value, raw bits, reinterpreted per the parameter's type.";
CM_ BO_ 1314 "TOOL -> DRIVE1 parameter/service request. OPCODE: 1 GET, 2 SET, 3 SAVE, 4 RESTORE_DEFAULTS, 5 INFO, 6 LOG_READ, 7 LOG_CLEAR. VALUE_RAW holds the SET value, raw bits, reinterpreted per the parameter's type.";
CM_ BO_ 1316 "DRIVE1 -> ORIN parameter/service response. STATUS: 0 OK, 1 bad index, 2 out of range, 3 not allowed while armed, 4 flash error. VALUE_RAW holds the current value, raw bits.";
CM_ BO_ 1317 "DRIVE1 -> RPI parameter/service response. STATUS: 0 OK, 1 bad index, 2 out of range, 3 not allowed while armed, 4 flash error. VALUE_RAW holds the current value, raw bits.";
CM_ BO_ 1318 "DRIVE1 -> TOOL parameter/service response. STATUS: 0 OK, 1 bad index, 2 out of range, 3 not allowed while armed, 4 flash error. VALUE_RAW holds the current value, raw bits.";
CM_ BO_ 1568 "DRIVE1 heartbeat, 10 Hz. NODE_TYPE: 1 drive, 2 arm, 3 science, 4 FPGA, 5 power. CAN_ERROR_STATE: 0 active, 1 passive, 2 recovered from bus-off.";
CM_ BO_ 1824 "Host -> DRIVE1 bootloader / firmware transfer (ISO-TP). Only while DRIVE1 is disarmed.";
CM_ BO_ 1825 "DRIVE1 -> host bootloader / firmware transfer (ISO-TP).";
